concept interfaces {
  name = "Interfaces"
  summary = "Structural contracts — a set of fields a type must have, satisfied automatically."
  related = [references]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p <<DOC
      An `interface` declares a structural contract — a set of fields a type must have to satisfy
      it. Any type with the right fields satisfies it automatically, with no explicit `implements`.
    DOC
    h2 "Declaring an interface"
    code "wcl" {
      source = <<DOC
        interface Drawable {
          x: f64
          y: f64
        }

        interface Sized extends Drawable {
          width:  f64
          height: f64
        }
      DOC
    }
    callout "Structural, not nominal" {
      class = ["info"]
      body = "A type need not be declared as a parent or implement anything explicitly. If it happens to have all the interface's fields with compatible types, it satisfies the interface."
    }
    p <<DOC
      Interfaces have one common consumer: **reference fields** (`&T`), which accept any value that
      structurally satisfies the interface. See [References](concept_references).
    DOC
  }
}
